#. §3: `hU : isOpen U`
#. §4: `hf.isOpen_preimage U hU`
#. §5: `isOpen (f ⁻¹' U)`
#: Game.Levels.Continuous.L01_continuous
msgid "The typeclass §0 is defined as follows:\n"
"\n"
"§1\n"
"\n"
"If you have hypotheses §2 and §3, then §4 is a proof of §5."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `exact`
#. §1: `exact`
#. §2: `h1`
#. §3: `x ∈ A`
#. §4: `x ∈ B`
#: Game.Levels.Subset.L02subhyp
msgid "This example is a better illustration of how the §0 tactic is usually\n"
"used.  Often §1 is followed by an expression that combines assumptions\n"
"to prove the goal.  In later levels, we will see other ways in which\n"
"assumptions can be combined to prove a goal.\n"
"\n"
"Note that in this proof, §2 could be thought of as a function that can be\n"
"applied to a proof of any statement of the form §3 to produce a proof\n"
"of §4.  Many proofs in Lean behave like functions."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `«{hf}».isOpen_preimage`
#. §1: `«{hg}».isOpen_preimage`
#: Game.Levels.Continuous.L02_is_continuous
msgid "Again, you can use §0 and §1 to finish the proof."
