#. §1: `«{x}» ∈ A`
#. §2: `«{x}» ∈ B`
#. §3: `«{x}» ∈ C`
#. §4: `with`
#. §5: `rcases`
#: Game.Levels.Union.L03cases
msgid "Now you have *two* goals.  For the first, the assumption §0 has been\n"
"replaced with §1, and for the second it has been replaced with §2.  In both\n"
"cases, you must prove §3.  The two identifiers after §4 in the §5 tactic\n"
"are used as the identifiers of the new assumptions in the two cases."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `A`
#. §1: `B`
#. §2: `A`
#. §3: `B`
#. §4: `A ∩ B`
#. §5: `A ∩ B`
#. §6: `A`
#. §7: `B`
#. §8: `A`
#. §9: `B`
#. §10: `A ∩ B`
#: Game.Levels.Inter
msgid "If §0 and §1 are sets, then the *intersection* of §2 and §3, denoted\n"
"§4, is the set of elements that the two sets have in common.  In other words,\n"
"for an object to be an element of §5, it must be an element of both §6 and §7.\n"
"\n"
"For example, if §8 is the set of all round things, and §9 is the set of all red things,\n"
"then §10 is the set of all round red things.\n"
"\n"
"In this world you'll prove some basic properties of intersections of sets."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `F`
#. §1: `U`
#. §2: `F`
#. §3: `U`
#. §4: `F`
#: Game.Levels.FamUnion
msgid "If §0 is a family of sets from §1, then the *union* of §2 is the set of all objects from\n"
"§3 that belong to at least one element of §4.  We'll investigate unions of families in this\n"
"world."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `x : U`
#. §1: `A : Set U`
#. §2: `B : Set U`
#. §3: `mem_union x A B`
#. §4: `x ∈ A ∪ B ↔ x ∈ A ∨ x ∈ B`
