#: Game.Levels.FamInter
msgid "So far the elements of all of our sets have been objects in the universe §0.  But\n"
"sets can contain other kinds of objects!  In the next two worlds, we will work with sets whose\n"
"elements are *sets of objects from §1*.  We will call these *families of sets* from §2.  To\n"
"indicate that §3 is a family of sets from §4, we write §5.\n"
"\n"
"For example, suppose §6 contains the people in a certain club, and we want to form a committee\n"
"consisting of five members of the club.  The set of all possible committees is a family\n"
"of sets from §7.  Each element of this family is a set containing five club members.\n"
"\n"
"Families of sets are sets, and everything you've learned about sets applies to families of sets.\n"
"For example, if you have §8 and §9, then §10 is a proof\n"
"of the statement §11.  Similarly, §12 is a proof of\n"
"§13, and §14 is a proof of §15.\n"
"\n"
"In this world we extend the idea of intersections to families of sets.  If §16 is a family of\n"
