"### If you have an assumption §12\n"
"\n"
"If §13 stands for some object, then §14 is a proof of §15.  Note that §16 must be the right\n"
"*type* of object.  For example, if §17 stands for an object in the universe §18, then §19 must\n"
"have type §20; if §21 stands for a set of objects from the universe §22, then §23 must have\n"
"type §24."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rewrite`
#. §1: `rewrite [mem_compl_iff]`
#. §2: `mem_compl_iff`
#. §3: `mem_compl_iff`
#. §4: `A`
#. §5: `«{x}»`
#. §6: `rewrite [mem_compl_iff] at «{h2}»`
#. §7: `«{h2}»`
#. §8: `mem_compl_iff`
#. §9: `B`
#. §10: `«{x}»`
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L03compsub
msgid "The §0 tactic is smart enough to figure out some things on its own.  If you\n"
"had just written §1, then Lean would have figured out how to apply the\n"
"theorem §2 to get an equivalence that could be used to make a replacement in the goal.\n"
"In other words, it would have figured out that the theorem §3 had to be applied to\n"
"§4 and §5.\n"
"\n"
"Similarly, you can write §6 to write out the meaning of §7.  Lean\n"
"will figure out that in this case, §8 has to be applied to §9 and §10."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Functions.L06_preimage_union
#: Game.Levels.Functions.L07_preimage_intersection
msgid "Try to solve it using what you've learned so far! Hints are available if you get stuck."
msgstr ""

#. §0: $f \\colon X \\to Y$
#. §1: $U \\subset Y$
#. §2: $f^{-1}(U)$
#: Game.Levels.Continuous.L01_continuous
msgid "If §0 and §1 is closed, then §2 is closed."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `obtain`
#. §1: `«{h}»`
#: Game.Levels.Functions.L11_composition
msgid "As usual when dealing with images, you can use §0 to unwrap the hypothesis §1."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `h2 : x ∉ B`
#. §1: `h2 : ¬x ∈ B`
#. §2: `x ∈ B`
#. §3: `x ∈ B → False`
#. §4: `«{h4}» : x ∈ B`
#. §5: `exact h2 «{h4}»`
#: Game.Levels.Comp.L01contra
msgid "You can think of §0 (which is shorthand for §1)\n"
"as meaning \"if §2 were true, then that would lead to a contradiction\"--in other\n"
"words, §3.\n"
"Applying this to your new assumption §4 will give the contradiction\n"
"you need.  In other words, §5 will close the goal."
msgstr ""
